;    1: TDecorate(count=4, unk2=4294967295, unk3=4294967295, unk4=0, unk5=1, unk6=0, unk7=4294967295, unk8=, ruby=ごうおん, unk10=4294967295, unk11=4294967295)
;    2: TDecorate(count=16, unk2=255, unk3=4294967295, unk4=0, unk5=3, unk6=0, unk7=4294967295, unk8=, ruby=, unk10=4294967295, unk11=4294967295)
;    3: TDecorate(count=3, unk2=4294967295, unk3=4294967295, unk4=0, unk5=1, unk6=0, unk7=4294967295, unk8=, ruby=しんぴょうせい, unk10=4294967295, unk11=4294967295)
; Display conditions:
;    0: TWdCondition(count=1253, target=)
; Links:
;    0: TWdLink(count=1161, event=, unk3=)
;---------------------------------------
; BEGIN DECOMPILED SCRIPT
;---------------------------------------
<SCENARIO VER="105">
<EVENT VALUE="MOTION\r\n789\r\nムービー\r\n11\r\n0\r\n1000\r\nNORMAL\r\nPASS">
{PLAYSND "in_dream低.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
<EVENT VALUE="STOPMOVIE">
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{CREATECG "文字カウント画像" "グラフィック\システム\文字カウント画像.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
<TXSPN>The video you just saw is nighttime footage shot in a certain city in Japan.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
The video contains footage of a residential area, a man's voice, and a strange <STYLE ID="1" RUBY="ごうおん">roar</STYLE> echoing through it all.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
According to the poster, there was nothing near them that could have been the source of this sound.<PG>
In fact, this sound is not limited to Japan.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\世界地図.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
In recent years, around the world, there has been one report after another of a <STYLE ID="1" RUBY="ごうおん">roar</STYLE> like grinding metal, or like a low trumpet blast, ringing out over a whole area.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Air currents in underground caverns, the sound of meteors, air currents high in the sky: many causes have been suggested, but no clear cause is known.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
This sound has been given a name.<PG>
{STOPSND "BGM" "0" "PASS"}
{DELETECG "000" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0"}
<STYLE ID="2">―The Apocalyptic Sound.</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "エデンの桜\BGM_212.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{PLAYMOVIE "悪天候.wmv" "256" "C" "C" "REPEAT" "FALSE" "0" "0"}
<EVENT VALUE="MOTION\r\n789\r\nムービー\r\n11\r\n255\r\n3000\r\nNORMAL\r\nPASS">
{WAIT "3000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
<EVENT VALUE="MOTION\r\n789\r\nムービー\r\n11\r\n255\r\n0\r\nNORMAL\r\nPASS">
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
The apocalyptic sound is also said to be a prophecy of destruction.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Each time the trumpet sounds, cataclysms occur, driving humanity toward extinction.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
The concept of the apocalyptic sound has been documented since about 2,000 years ago, and it has a religious aspect.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Religious scholar Kevin White puts it this way.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
<EVENT VALUE="MOTION\r\n789\r\nムービー\r\n11\r\n0\r\n500\r\nNORMAL\r\nPASS">
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\ケビンホワイト.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
<EVENT VALUE="STOPMOVIE">
{MESON "500"}
"Religion, along with agriculture, is an element at the very root of human culture. In other words, it's no exaggeration to say culture equals religion. 
{PAUSE ""}
Why could religion become such an element? Because in the past, science was not as developed as it is today. 
{PAUSE ""}
When people encountered something mysterious whose cause they didn't understand, they couldn't help feeling uneasy. 
{PAUSE ""}
Religion was needed to explain it."<PG>
"What happens to people when they die? 
{PAUSE ""}
Why does the sun rise? 
{PAUSE ""}
Why does night come? 
{PAUSE ""}
Why do storms happen? 
{PAUSE ""}
And why do sounds like the apocalyptic sound ring out? 
{PAUSE ""}
From familiar things like these to the very rare, people explained them through religion. 
{PAUSE ""}
And when many people believe in that religion, group psychology increases the <STYLE ID="3" RUBY="しんぴょうせい">credibility</STYLE> of the explanation. 
{PAUSE ""}
This is one of the reasons a particular religion spreads widely."<PG>
"In other words, this gives us a hypothesis. 
{PAUSE ""}
That is: 'The occurrence of the apocalyptic sound will bring about the destruction of humanity' 
{PAUSE ""}
―the apocalyptic sound was being observed as long as 2,000 years ago. 
{PAUSE ""}
We can say that people, seeking to explain that eerie, inexplicable sound, turned to religion for salvation."<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYMOVIE "悪天候.wmv" "256" "C" "C" "REPEAT" "FALSE" "100" "0"}
<EVENT VALUE="MOTION\r\n789\r\nムービー\r\n11\r\n255\r\n3000\r\nNORMAL\r\nPASS">
{WAIT "3000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
<EVENT VALUE="MOTION\r\n789\r\nムービー\r\n11\r\n255\r\n0\r\nNORMAL\r\nPASS">
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
According to Kevin White, the apocalyptic sound is not something observed only recently; its existence has been recognized for as long as 2,000 years.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Today we live in an information society, where information from all over the world is instantly available.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Phenomena like the apocalyptic sound can also be recorded as video and shared with people around the world.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
That is why people all over the world today can know of the apocalyptic sound's existence.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
<EVENT VALUE="MOTION\r\n789\r\nムービー\r\n11\r\n0\r\n500\r\nNORMAL\r\nPASS">
{WAIT "500" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
<EVENT VALUE="STOPMOVIE">
{MESON "500"}
"Until now, science has explained many mysterious phenomena. 
{PAUSE ""}
Surely the apocalyptic sound, too, will turn out to be caused by some natural phenomenon or by a phenomenon of human perception. 
{PAUSE ""}
Once the apocalyptic sound is explained, that video will probably become something people laugh about."
{WAIT "100" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{DELETECG "文字カウント画像" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0"}
<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{STOPSND "BGM" "3000" "PASS"}
{DELETECG "000,111" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
<PG>
{}
<EVENT VALUE="MESEND">
